+/// Get shared mobile TUN settings for a JSON array of instance UUID strings.
+///
+/// Uses the same instance manager as local and config-server instances. The
+/// returned JSON contains `instance_ids`, `addresses`, `routes`, `dns`, and
+/// per-member `rejected` errors. Conflicting members do not displace unchanged
+/// attached members. Only Android and iOS support this operation.
+///
+/// Returns an allocated JSON string, or null on failure. Release it with
+/// `free_string`; retrieve failures with `get_error_msg` on the same thread.
+/// Do not call this from a config-server event callback.
+///
+/// # Safety
+/// `instance_ids_json` must point to a NUL-terminated UTF-8 JSON array.
